module std where

-- tryParseBoolean — Attempt to parse a string as a
-- Boolean. ∀. String → Maybe Boolean.
--
-- The .fenel-side function name is `tryParseBooleanFn`,
-- NOT `tryParseBoolean`. `tryParseBoolean` itself is
-- not a parser reserved keyword (probed — no LHS
-- rejection), but the `Fn`-suffix matches the
-- 5b6/5b7/5b8 convention for hybrid TS-native-deletion
-- ports (treats the .fenel-side body as a "back-end"
-- function distinct from the user-facing
-- `tryParseBoolean` codeName). std.ts extracts via
-- `f.id === "std-tryParseBoolean:tryParseBooleanFn"`
-- and wires the body into the `std:tryParseBoolean`
-- spec; the user-facing codeName stays
-- `tryParseBoolean`.
--
-- Pre-5b9 the spec was TS-native via
-- `stdNatives.tryParseBoolean = (s) => { ... ; return
-- null }` at engine/src/modules/std.ts:3030. The TS
-- native returned non-conformant `true | false | null`
-- where the spec declares `returns: Maybe(Boolean)` —
-- AGENTS.md says `null` is BANNED in Fenel (absence is
-- `Nothing`). Post-5b9 the spec gains a body returning
-- the conformant `{$tag: "Just", value: true | false}
-- | {$tag: "Nothing"}` shape and the
-- `stdNatives.tryParseBoolean` entry is deleted.
-- Spec-conformance bug retired.
--
-- 5b9 introduces a NEW workaround tier — bundled
-- downstream refactor. 5b6/5b7 diverged the .fenel-
-- side ident only; 5b8 renamed the SPEC's own params.
-- Both stayed CONFINED to std.ts. 5b9 spans std.ts
-- AND a downstream caller at
-- engine/src/modules/telegram.ts:1417 in one commit —
-- the pre-5b9 match pattern there used raw `null` as
-- the no-match case AND bare `{$bind: "b"}` for the
-- Just case (relying on the non-conformant return).
-- Post-5b9 it consumes the canonical Maybe-variant
-- shape: `{$tag: "Nothing"}` + `{$tag: "Just", value:
-- {$bind: "b"}}`. Establishes the bundled-downstream-
-- refactor workaround tier (matching-name → .fenel
-- ident divergence → spec-param rename → bundled-
-- downstream-refactor) for future spec-conformance
-- ports where the TS native returns a non-conformant
-- shape that downstream callers rely on.
--
-- Body calls into `elem` / `lower` / `trim` — all
-- three are std TS-natives that stay TS-native
-- (string-ops Phase 6+ tooling dep). Same Fenel-body-
-- calling-TS-native chain as 5b4's `count → length`
-- and `appendItem → concat`.
--
-- Parens around `True` / `False` are REQUIRED — bare
-- `Just True` parses to `{construct: ["Just", {var:
-- "True"}]}` (True interpreted as identifier in
-- argument position). `Just (True)` parses correctly
-- to `{construct: ["Just", {construct: ["True"]}]}`.

@label "Try parse boolean"
@description "Attempt to parse a string as a Boolean. Recognises yes/y/true/1/ok/yep/yeah → Just true and no/n/false/0/nope/nah → Just false (case-insensitive, trimmed). Returns Nothing for anything else. Conformant Maybe(Boolean) return shape (Phase 5b9 — pre-5b9 the TS native returned non-conformant `null` for the unknown case; callers using legacy `match [_, null, ...]` patterns must update to `match [_, {$tag: \"Nothing\"}, ...]`)."
@tags "parse" "boolean" "input"
tryParseBoolean : (s: String) -> Maybe Boolean
tryParseBoolean s =
  if elem (lower (trim s)) ["yes", "y", "true", "1", "ok", "yep", "yeah"]
    then Just (True)
    else if elem (lower (trim s)) ["no", "n", "false", "0", "nope", "nah"]
      then Just (False)
      else Nothing
